# Session Log — Azure Load Balancer Lab

## Session Objective

Build and troubleshoot an Azure Standard Public Load Balancer using two Ubuntu VMs as backend servers.

Primary focus:

- Azure CLI commands
- Resource creation
- Network configuration
- NSG configuration
- Load Balancer configuration
- Health probes
- Backend pool
- Load-balancing rules
- Traffic testing
- Backend failure/recovery
- Outbound SNAT
- Default outbound access
- VM lifecycle troubleshooting
- Final connectivity validation


============================================================
1. RESOURCE GROUP
============================================================

Created the lab resource group.

Command:

az group create `
  -n az-lb-lab-rg `
  -l centralindia `
  --tags owner=tarun AutoDelete=Yes


============================================================
2. VIRTUAL NETWORK
============================================================

Created the VNet and first subnet.

Command:

az network vnet create `
  -g az-lb-lab-rg `
  -l centralindia `
  -n az-lb-lab-vnet `
  --address-prefixes 10.10.0.0/16 `
  --subnet-name az-lb-lab-subnet1 `
  --subnet-prefixes 10.10.1.0/24 `
  --tags owner=tarun


Created the second subnet.

Command:

az network vnet subnet create `
  -g az-lb-lab-rg `
  --vnet-name az-lb-lab-vnet `
  -n az-lb-lab-subnet2 `
  --address-prefixes 10.10.2.0/24


Verified the subnets.

Command:

az network vnet subnet list `
  -g az-lb-lab-rg `
  --vnet-name az-lb-lab-vnet `
  --query "[].{Subnet:name,Prefix:addressPrefix}" `
  -o table


Expected:

Subnet                 Prefix
---------------------  -------------
az-lb-lab-subnet1      10.10.1.0/24
az-lb-lab-subnet2      10.10.2.0/24


============================================================
3. BACKEND VMs
============================================================

Created VM1 in subnet1.

Command:

az vm create `
  -g az-lb-lab-rg `
  -n az-lb-lab-vm1 `
  -l centralindia `
  --image Ubuntu2204 `
  --size Standard_D2s_v5 `
  --vnet-name az-lb-lab-vnet `
  --subnet az-lb-lab-subnet1 `
  --admin-username azureuser `
  --generate-ssh-keys `
  --public-ip-sku Standard `
  --tags owner=tarun


VM1:

Name:
az-lb-lab-vm1

Private IP:
10.10.1.4


Created VM2 in subnet2.

