============================================================
20. LOAD BALANCER OUTBOUND RULE
============================================================

Created an outbound rule.

Command:

az network lb outbound-rule create `
  -g az-lb-lab-rg `
  --lb-name az-lb-lab-lb `
  -n az-lb-lab-outbound `
  --protocol All `
  --frontend-ip-configs az-lb-lab-frontend `
  --backend-pool az-lb-lab-lbbepool `
  --idle-timeout 15 `
  --allocated-outbound-ports 1024 `
  --enable-tcp-reset true


The initial creation attempt failed.

Azure returned:

LoadBalancingRuleMustDisableSNATSinceSameFrontendIPConfigurationIsReferencedByOutboundRule


The existing load-balancing rule was updated to disable outbound
SNAT:

Command:

az network lb rule update `
  -g az-lb-lab-rg `
  --lb-name az-lb-lab-lb `
  -n az-lb-lab-http-rule `
  --disable-outbound-snat true


The outbound rule was then created successfully.


Verified the outbound rule:

Command:

az network lb outbound-rule show `
  -g az-lb-lab-rg `
  --lb-name az-lb-lab-lb `
  -n az-lb-lab-outbound `
  --query "{Name:name,Protocol:protocol,IdleTimeout:idleTimeoutInMinutes,AllocatedPorts:allocatedOutboundPorts,Frontend:frontendIPConfigurations[].id,BackendPool:backendAddressPool.id}" `
  -o json


Result:

{
